---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/shared/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Layout title="Agent Dev Server | Astro Lab" description="Astro 7 agent-friendly dev server with background mode and JSON logs">
	<div class="space-y-8">
		<header class="text-center">
			<span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-purple-400 mb-4">Astro 7</span>
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Agent Dev Server</h1>
			<p class="text-lg text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
				Astro 7 is the first framework with first-class AI agent support.
				Background dev server, structured JSON logs, health endpoints, and automatic agent detection.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="rounded-xl border border-purple-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-purple-500/10 to-blue-500/10 p-6">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Astro &times; Claude Code</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-300">
				This entire site was built and migrated using Claude Code as the primary development agent.
				Astro 7's agent dev server features made this workflow seamless — background mode means
				the dev server runs without blocking the terminal, JSON logs are parseable by AI agents,
				and the health endpoint lets agents verify the server state programmatically.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Background Mode</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-400">
				Start the dev server in the background — it returns control to your terminal (or AI agent) immediately:
			</p>
			<CodeBlock title="Terminal" lang="bash">
{`# Start in background
astro dev --background

# Check status
astro dev status

# View logs
astro dev logs --follow

# Stop the server
astro dev stop`}
			</CodeBlock>
			<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
				The background process persists across terminal sessions. PID and port are tracked
				automatically — no manual process management needed.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Health Endpoint</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-400">
				The dev server exposes <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">/_astro/status</code>
				for programmatic health checks:
			</p>
			<CodeBlock title="GET /_astro/status" lang="json">
{`{
  "status": "ready",
  "version": "7.0.9",
  "port": 4321,
  "uptime": 142.5,
  "routes": 22,
  "errors": 0
}`}
			</CodeBlock>
			<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
				AI agents can poll this endpoint to know when the server is ready before
				running tests or making requests. No more <code class="font-mono">sleep 5</code>
				and hoping for the best.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Agent Detection</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-400">
				Astro automatically detects when it's being run by an AI coding agent and
				adjusts its output format:
			</p>
			<CodeBlock title="How detection works" lang="text">
{`# Astro checks for the presence of AI agent indicators:
# - Environment variables set by Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, etc.
# - The "am-i-vibing" signal (a community convention)
# - Terminal capabilities that suggest non-human operation

# When an agent is detected:
# - Output switches to structured JSON (parseable logs)
# - Interactive prompts are auto-answered with safe defaults
# - Error messages include file paths and line numbers for programmatic fixing`}
			</CodeBlock>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">JSON Structured Logs</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-400">
				When running in agent mode or with <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">--json</code>,
				all log output is structured JSON — one object per line:
			</p>
			<CodeBlock title="JSON log output" lang="json">
{`{"level":"info","msg":"Server started","port":4321,"timestamp":"2026-07-15T12:00:00Z"}
{"level":"info","msg":"GET /","status":200,"duration_ms":12,"timestamp":"2026-07-15T12:00:01Z"}
{"level":"warn","msg":"Deprecation","file":"src/pages/old.astro","line":5,"timestamp":"2026-07-15T12:00:02Z"}
{"level":"error","msg":"Build error","file":"src/pages/broken.astro","line":12,"col":8,"timestamp":"2026-07-15T12:00:03Z"}`}
			</CodeBlock>
			<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
				AI agents can parse these logs line-by-line, detect errors, and fix them
				without needing to parse ANSI escape codes or human-readable formatting.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800 p-6">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Agent Workflow Example</h2>
			<p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">
				A typical Claude Code workflow with Astro 7:
			</p>
			<div class="space-y-3">
				<div class="flex gap-3">
					<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 text-sm font-bold text-purple-400">1</span>
					<div>
						<p class="font-medium text-white">Start dev server</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-400"><code class="font-mono">astro dev --background</code> — returns immediately, agent continues working</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flex gap-3">
					<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 text-sm font-bold text-purple-400">2</span>
					<div>
						<p class="font-medium text-white">Wait for ready</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Poll <code class="font-mono">/_astro/status</code> until <code class="font-mono">"status": "ready"</code></p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flex gap-3">
					<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 text-sm font-bold text-purple-400">3</span>
					<div>
						<p class="font-medium text-white">Make changes</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Edit files — HMR updates automatically, JSON logs report any errors</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flex gap-3">
					<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 text-sm font-bold text-purple-400">4</span>
					<div>
						<p class="font-medium text-white">Verify</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Fetch pages, check responses, run <code class="font-mono">astro check</code></p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flex gap-3">
					<span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-500/20 text-sm font-bold text-purple-400">5</span>
					<div>
						<p class="font-medium text-white">Clean up</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-400"><code class="font-mono">astro dev stop</code> — no orphan processes</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>
